hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2872","Narrated to us ‘Ali ibn Khashram: narrated to us ‘Isa, from Ibn Jurayj, who informed me—‘Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid— that he heard Ibn ‘Abbas (RA) say:\n“I was among those whom the Prophet (ﷺ) sent ahead with the baggage from Muzdalifah to Mina at night.”\n\nSimilarly, narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma’mar: narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakr: Ibn Jurayj informed us with the same wording.\n\nAbu Bakr (ibn Abi Shaybah) said:\nThe reports of Ibn ‘Abbas (RA) stating that he was among those whom the Prophet (ﷺ) sent ahead with the baggage from Muzdalifah to Mina at night indicate that the one commanded to collect the pebbles in the morning of Muzdalifah is al-Fadl ibn ‘Abbas (RA), not ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Abbas (RA).\n\nMeanwhile, the reports of al-Fadl (RA) that he was the one mounted behind the Prophet (ﷺ) from Muzdalifah to Mina at night indicate that the report of Mushash from ‘Ata’ from Ibn ‘Abbas from al-Fadl stating that he was among those sent ahead is a mistake, because the one sent ahead with the weak from Muzdalifah to Mina is ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Abbas (RA), not al-Fadl.\n\nCHAPTER:"
